  "body": "createImageBitmap(CANVAS,4294967400, 4294967400, 4294967400, 4294967400);\r\nseems to create a imageBitmap of size 104.\r\n\r\nAccording to the WebIDL[1] spec: The long type is a signed integer type that has values in the range [−2147483648, 2147483647]\r\nThe conversion algorithm from JS number to long [2], uses a modulo operation to enforce the range, which means overflows simply wrap around.\r\n\r\nSince there are no warnings or errors, unintended results may occur.\r\n\r\nAccording to the HTML Standard[3], if either sw or sh is given and is 0, then return p rejected with a RangeError.\r\nI think we can use either EnforceRange extended attribute[4] or the Clamp extended attribute[5] for this issue as well.\r\n\r\n\r\n[1] https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-long\r\n[2] https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-toint32\r\n[3]https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/imagebitmap-and-animations.html#dom-createimagebitmap\r\n[4] https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#EnforceRange\r\n[5] https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#Clamp",
